	(text "# BATTERY SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (BATTERY BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet - COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe battery subsystem manages dynamic power-path routing, lithium battery charging, hardware power switching, state-of-charge fuel gauging, \n \\and edge ground probing. It utilizes a BQ24075 power-path manager (U4) to seamlessly power downstream regulators (VDD) \nfrom either USB Input (VBUS) or a single-cell LiPo/Li-Ion battery (+BATT). A MAX17048 fuel gauge (U5) provides battery telemetry over I2C, \nwhile a dedicated slide switch (S1) controls physical battery isolation.\n\n1. BATTERY CHARGER, POWER-PATH & POWER SWITCH (U4 BQ24075RGT)\n* Core IC: U4 (BQ24075RGT standalone Li-ion power-path manager).\n* Hardware Power Switch (S1): Slide switch S1 connected to pin 15 (SYSOFF). Toggling S1 switches SYSOFF between GND \n                            (normal battery operation / power ON) and +BATT (battery disconnect / system OFF).\n* Input Mode Configuration (EN1/EN2): Pin 5 (EN2) is pulled HIGH to VBUS through a 10kΩ resistor (R12), and Pin 6 (EN1) is tied LOW to GND. \n  Per Table 1 of the BQ24075 datasheet, this EN2=1, EN1=0 state configures External Resistor Mode via pin 12 (ILIM) \n  and ensures stable VDD passthrough during batteryless USB operation.\n* Input Current Limit: Resistor R13 (1.18kΩ) on pin 12 (ILIM) configures the programmable maximum input current draw from VBUS to 1.35A.\n* Fast-Charge Current: Resistor R14 (1.13kΩ) on pin 16 (ISET) sets fast-charge current to 787mA.\n* Input Decoupling: C10 (1µF) ceramic capacitor connected between VBUS input and GND.\n* Battery Terminal Connection: BAT pin (pin 2) connects to the single-cell battery rail +BATT, decoupled by C12 (4.7µF). \n  Connected to 3-pin battery connector J2 (BATT_CONN).\n* System Power Rail (VDD): OUT pin (pin 10) provides the main system output rail VDD, decoupled by C11 (4.7µF) and monitored by test point TP7.\n* Charge Enable: Pin 4 (~CE) pulled LOW to GND to enable automatic charging when VBUS is present.\n* Safety Timer: Pin 14 (TMR) tied to GND through R11 (46.4kΩ) to set safety timer limits.\n* Thermal Protection: Pin 1 (TS) tied to 10kΩ NTC thermistor TH1 on PCB as well as Pin 2 (NTC) of 3-pin J2 header \n  to suspend charging during over/under-temperature conditions. TH1 is designated DNP when using external pack NTC.\n* Status Monitors: PGOOD (pin 7) pulled up to +3.3V via R15 (10kΩ). CHG (pin 9) pulled up to +3.3V via R16 (10kΩ). \n  Static PCB power/alert LEDs (D3/D4) removed to eliminate continuous parasitic drain during deep sleep.\n\n2. FUEL GAUGE SETUP (U5 MAX17048G+T10)\n* Core IC: U5 (MAX17048G+T10 ModelGauge I2C fuel gauge).\n* Sensing & Power: CELL (pin 2) and VDD (pin 3) tied directly to the +BATT rail, decoupled by C13 (100nF).\n* Grounding: GND (pin 4), CTG (pin 1), and Exposed Pad EP (pin 9) connected directly to system GND.\n* I2C Telemetry: SCL (pin 7) and SDA (pin 8) routed to the shared I2C bus (I2C_BUS.SCL, I2C_BUS.SDA).\n* Interrupt Output: ALERT (pin 5) drives active-LOW BATT_ALERT signal directly to MCU GPIO21 for low-power wake-up triggers.\n* Quick-Start Pin: QSTRT (pin 6) tied to GND.\n\n3. PCB EDGE GROUNDING & TEST POINT ARRAY\n* Edge Ground Test Points: Dedicated test points TP3, TP4, TP5, and TP6 are placed at the perimeter/corners of the schematic layout.\n* Function: Provides reliable multimeter/oscilloscope ground clip attachment points across the PCB boundary \n  and facilitates chassis grounding checks without cluttering internal signal lines.\n\n4. INTERFACE MATRIX\n* VBUS: +5V power input supplied from the USB-C interface.\n* VDD: Regulated system power output driving downstream buck-boost converters (+3.3V / +3.3VA).\n* +BATT: Unregulated single-cell LiPo/Li-ion battery rail (3.0V to 4.2V nominal).\n* S1 (SWITCH): Hardware system power switch (toggles SYSOFF).\n* J2 (BATT_CONN): 3-pin header (+BATT, NTC, GND) for external battery pack interfacing.\n* TP3-TP6: PCB perimeter Ground (GND) test points."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
